  "answer_text": "Here is how you can log in to your **My Service Canada Account (MSCA)**:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd17 Direct Login Link\n\ud83d\udc49 **[Click here to sign in to My Service Canada Account (MSCA)](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html)**\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd10 How to Sign In\n\nYou can sign in using **one of the following methods:**\n\n1. **GCKey**\nGCKey allows you to access multiple Government of Canada online services.\n\n2. **Interac\u00ae Sign-In Partner (Banking credentials)**\nInterac\u00ae Sign-In Partner allows you to register or sign in using your online banking sign-in information to access MSCA.\n\n3. **Provincial Sign-In (Alberta & BC only)**\nYou can access My Service Canada Account (MSCA) by signing in or registering with your provincial sign-in. This service is only available for residents of Alberta and British Columbia.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccb New User? How to Register\n\nIf you don't have an account yet:\n- You can create a GCKey username and password by clicking \"Start your registration\" on the registration page.\n- The Interac\u00ae verification service allows you to verify your identity during your MSCA registration, and you will only have to complete this step once.\n- Personal Access Codes (PACs) are used to verify your identity when registering for MSCA. If you have already applied for CPP/OAS benefits, your PAC has been sent to you by mail.\n\n---\n\n### \u26a0\ufe0f Important Reminder\nYou must access and use MSCA only as yourself \u2014 no one is authorized to use or create an account on your behalf.\n\nIf you need further help, visit the official page: **https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html**",
